<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{question}</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"Below are the related passages:"</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{reference}</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"Below is an answer:"</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{response}</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"Your task is to determine whether the answer contains hallucinations."
"First, provide reasoning with the following format:"</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">## Step 1: <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> your first reasoning step <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">## Step 2: <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> your next reasoning step <math id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">…(add as many steps as needed)
Then, compile the labeled hallucinated spans into a JSON dict, with a key hallucination list and its value is a list of hallucinated spans. If there are potential hallucinations, the output should be in the following JSON format: hallucination list: [hallucination span1, hallucination span2, …]. Otherwise, leave the value as an empty list as follows: hallucination list: [].</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
